---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import legacyPages from '../../data/legacy-pages.json';
const page = legacyPages['blogs-portfolio-thinking'];
---

<SiteLayout {...page} legacy={true} noindex={false}>
  <main id="main" class="article-content">
    <nav class="article-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/blogs/"
        >Hiring &amp; career guides</a
      >
    </nav><p class="overline">Quantum Leaps · Practical guidance</p><h1>
      Show How You Think: A Better Portfolio Conversation
    </h1><p class="article-meta">
      By Quantum Leaps · Published and reviewed 25 October 2026 · 2 min read
    </p><p class="article-note">
      Make your contribution, constraints and decisions easy for a hiring team
      to understand.
    </p><h2>Start with relevant work</h2><p>
      Choose a small number of projects that relate to the role. Explain the
      audience, problem and constraints before showing the finished work. A
      clear account of a modest project can be more useful than a beautiful
      result with no explanation.
    </p><h2>Make your contribution explicit</h2><p>
      Describe what you owned, what others contributed and who made key
      decisions. Hiring teams should not have to guess whether you led the
      project, produced one part or supported delivery.
    </p><h2>Show a decision and its tradeoff</h2><p>
      Explain an alternative you considered and why you chose a different
      direction. Share what you learned from feedback or testing. Only use
      outcomes you can substantiate; if a result was not measured, say so.
    </p><h2>Respect confidentiality</h2><p>
      Use public work or material you have permission to share. Redact
      confidential business details and explain the limitation. Never upload
      client secrets simply to make a portfolio appear more impressive.
    </p><ul>
      <li>What was the problem?</li><li>
        What did you personally contribute?
      </li><li>Which constraint shaped the work?</li><li>
        What evidence supports the result?
      </li><li>What would you change next time?</li>
    </ul><p>
      <a href="/contact/">Discuss a hiring brief →</a> · <a href="/submit-cv/"
        >Share your CV →</a
      >
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
